/* The widget gallery — what somebody reads while choosing a widget to add.
   iOS renders that gallery before the widget has any data, so these cannot
   travel from the phone the way every other word in this extension does.
   They resolve here instead.

   Keys are the English text, because that is what .configurationDisplayName
   and .description receive. WidgetKit declares its plain-String overloads
   @_disfavoredOverload, so a literal binds to LocalizedStringKey and is looked
   up in this bundle — verified against the SDK interface, not assumed.

   This English file is not strictly required: a missing key resolves to the
   key, which is the English. It ships anyway so the bundle declares BOTH
   localizations. With only es.lproj present and no CFBundleDevelopmentRegion
   in Info.plist, Spanish is the bundle's sole localization and an English
   reader can be resolved into it. */

"Up Next" = "Up Next";
"Your next deadlines at a glance." = "Your next deadlines at a glance.";
"Due This Week" = "Due This Week";
"Everything due in the next 7 days, plus your streak." = "Everything due in the next 7 days, plus your streak.";
